ry 14, 2025"}]]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-[#dfbd8b]","children":["Updated ",["$","time",null,{"dateTime":"2026-11-20","children":"November 19, 2026"}]]}]]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"py-12 px-6 md:px-14","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-3xl mx-auto","children":[["$","nav",null,{"aria-label":"Table of Contents","className":"mb-10 p-6 bg-black-2 border border-orange-DEFAULT/25","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[0.52rem] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-orange-DEFAULT mb-3","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":13,"height":13,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-book-open","children":[["$","path","vv98re",{"d":"M2 3h6a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v14a3 3 0 0 0-3-3H2z"}],["$","path","1cyq3y",{"d":"M22 3h-6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v14a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h7z"}],"$undefined"]}],"In This Guide"]}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-2","children":[["$","li","the-law-of-attraction-vs-the-law-of-assumption",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#the-law-of-attraction-vs-the-law-of-assumption","className":"font-body text-sm text-grey-DEFAULT hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors flex items-baseline gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.5rem] text-orange-DEFAULT/80","children":["01","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The Law of Attraction vs. The Law of Assumption"}]]}]}],["$","li","what-assumption-actually-means",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#what-assumption-actually-means","className":"font-body text-sm text-grey-DEFAULT hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors flex items-baseline gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.5rem] text-orange-DEFAULT/80","children":["02","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"What \"Assumption\" Actually Means"}]]}]}],["$","li","why-most-people-fail",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#why-most-people-fail","className":"font-body text-sm text-grey-DEFAULT hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors flex items-baseline gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.5rem] text-orange-DEFAULT/80","children":["03","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Why Most People Fail"}]]}]}],["$","li","the-role-of-your-brain",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#the-role-of-your-brain","className":"font-body text-sm text-grey-DEFAULT hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors flex items-baseline gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.5rem] text-orange-DEFAULT/80","children":["04","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The Role of Your Brain"}]]}]}],["$","li","how-to-begin",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#how-to-begin","className":"font-body text-sm text-grey-DEFAULT hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors flex items-baseline gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.5rem] text-orange-DEFAULT/80","children":["05","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"How to Begin"}]]}]}]]}]]}],[["$","h2","0",{"id":"the-law-of-attraction-vs-the-law-of-assumption","className":"scroll-mt-24 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"The Law of Attraction vs. The Law of Assumption"}],["$","p","1",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["Most people come to Neville Goddard through the Law of Attraction. They've tried vision boards, gratitude journals, and positive affirmations. Some things worked. Most didn't. And the inconsistency was maddening."]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["Neville's teaching is different at the root level. The Law of Attraction says: ",["$","em","1",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"think about what you want and it will come to you."}]," The Law of Assumption says: ",["$","em","3",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"assume you already have it, and reality will rearrange itself to confirm that assumption."}],""]}],["$","p","3",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["The distinction sounds subtle. It is not."]}],["$","h2","4",{"id":"what-assumption-actually-means","className":"scroll-mt-24 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"What \"Assumption\" Actually Means"}],["$","p","5",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["To assume, in Neville's framework, is to occupy a state. Not to pretend. Not to lie to yourself. But to step into the consciousness of a person who already has what you desire — and ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"feel from that place."}],""]}],["$","p","6",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["Imagine you've just received the news that you got the job. Or that the relationship is healed. Or that the money arrived. How does that ",["$","em","1",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"feel"}]," in your body? That feeling — that specific inner tone — is the assumption. And according to Neville, that feeling is a cause, not an effect."]}],["$","blockquote","7",{"className":"border-l-2 border-orange-DEFAULT pl-6 my-8 font-body italic text-grey-DEFAULT text-lg leading-relaxed","children":["",["$","em","1",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"\"Assume the feeling of your wish fulfilled and observe the route that your attention follows.\""}]," — Neville Goddard"]}],["$","h2","8",{"id":"why-most-people-fail","className":"scroll-mt-24 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"Why Most People Fail"}],["$","p","9",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["The most common mistake is \"thinking of\" rather than \"thinking from.\" You think ",["$","em","1",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"about"}]," the desired outcome as something distant, something to be obtained. But Neville teaches that you must think ",["$","em","3",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"from"}]," the state — as if it is already done."]}],["$","p","10",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["This is not semantics. It rewires the instruction being sent to the subconscious."]}],["$","p","11",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["When you think ",["$","em","1",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"of"}]," something, your subconscious registers lack. When you think ",["$","em","3",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"from"}]," it — as a living reality — your subconscious registers fulfillment and begins filtering the world for evidence to confirm it."]}],["$","h2","12",{"id":"the-role-of-your-brain","className":"scroll-mt-24 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"The Role of Your Brain"}],["$","p","13",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["Neuroscience gives us a framework to understand why this works. Your Reticular Activating System (RAS) — a network in the brainstem — filters approximately 11 million bits of incoming data per second, allowing only 50 into conscious awareness. It filters for what you've told it is important."]}],["$","p","14",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["When you deeply assume a state — emotionally, not just intellectually — you reprogram the RAS to select for evidence of that state in the world around you. Opportunities appear. Coincidences multiply. The \"bridge of incidents\" forms."]}],["$","h2","15",{"id":"how-to-begin","className":"scroll-mt-24 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"How to Begin"}],["$","ol","16",{"className":"flex flex-col gap-3 my-6","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-orange-DEFAULT text-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5","children":["01","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"Identify the specific desire."}]," Not a vague wish, but a precise outcome."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-orange-DEFAULT text-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5","children":["02","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"Create a brief scene"}]," that implies the wish fulfilled — a single moment ",["$","em","3",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"after"}]," the desire has manifested."]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-orange-DEFAULT text-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5","children":["03","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"Inhabit the feeling"}]," of that scene nightly, especially in the state akin to sleep (SATS)."]}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-orange-DEFAULT text-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5","children":["04","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"Persist."}]," Current reality is an echo of past thoughts. Stay faithful to the assumption even when 3D shows no confirmation."]}]]}]]}],["$","p","17",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["The Law of Assumption is not a technique. It is an understanding of how consciousness creates reality. And once you've seen it work — even once — the world never looks the same again."]}]],["$","section",null,{"aria-labelledby":"faq-heading","className":"mt-16 pt-10 border-t border-white/10","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[0.52rem] tracking-[0.25em] uppercase text-orange-DEFAULT mb-2","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":13,"height":13,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle-help","children":[["$","circle","1mglay",{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"}],["$","path","1u773s",{"d":"M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3"}],["$","path","p32p05",{"d":"M12 17h.01"}],"$undefined"]}],"Key Questions Answered"]}],["$","h2",null,{"id":"faq-heading","className":"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mb-6","children":"FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"bg-black-2 border border-white/10 p-6 hover:border-orange-DEFAULT/30 transition-colors","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-body font-semibold text-white text-base mb-2","children":"What is the main difference between the Law of Assumption and the Law of Attraction?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT text-sm leading-relaxed","children":"The Law of Attraction often focuses on trying to attract something external toward you through positive thinking, which can subtly reinforce the feeling that you do not have it yet. The Law of Assumption teaches that consciousness is the only reality: when you inwardly assume and occupy the feeling of already being the person whose wish is fulfilled, your perception, behavior, and external reality reorganize to match that ass